Post 5: AI/ML Ops Engineer Interview  
Fresher Level (0–1 Year)

The hottest role in tech right now — **AI/ML Ops** where DevOps meets Machine Learning! 🔥  
MLOps Engineers bridge data scientists and production infrastructure to deploy AI models at scale.  

If you're starting in this exciting space, these foundational questions will get you interview-ready 👇  

💡 Common AI/ML Ops Interview Questions for Freshers:
1️⃣ What is **MLOps**, and how does it differ from traditional DevOps?  
2️⃣ Explain the key stages of the **ML lifecycle** (data prep → training → deployment → monitoring).  
3️⃣ What tools are commonly used for **model versioning** (e.g., MLflow, DVC)?  
4️⃣ How do you containerize ML models for deployment (Docker + inference servers)?  
5️⃣ What is **model drift**, and why does it matter in production?  
6️⃣ Explain the difference between **batch inference** and **real-time inference**.  
7️⃣ How would you deploy a simple ML model using **Kubernetes** or serverless platforms?  
8️⃣ What role does **CI/CD** play in the MLOps workflow?  
9️⃣ How do you monitor ML models in production (accuracy, latency, data drift)?  
🔟 What are some challenges in scaling ML inference across multiple GPUs?  

🎯 Pro Tip:  
Start with a **simple end-to-end project** — train a model with scikit-learn, containerize it, deploy to cloud, and add basic monitoring.  
Hands-on MLOps demos > theoretical knowledge every time! 🧪  
